   "speech": "“I sit, I think… About what? About eternity, death, the mystery of the universe, space… well, about everything that creeps into your head after a hearty supper and strong tea… I remember the philosophers, various theories, conversations… And one thing came back to me, from my childhood days… I was very proud of it then, that I had arrived at it, so to speak, by my own wits. This is how I reasoned: an infinite amount of time went by before ‘I’ appeared… Well, sir, I die, and let us suppose I never existed at all… And so — why, within the bounds of infinity, can I not appear again? I put it a little confusedly, of course… but an example… like this… a clean sheet of paper, say, here. I take a pencil and write 10. And now — I go and rub it out completely, clean away… And what then! I take the pencil again and write ‘10’ again. You understand — a 1 and a 0.”",
